Продолжи проектирование LiveSpec vNext, но не начинай реализацию.

Работай read-only. Не редактируй репозиторий, не создавай worktree, не запускай full suite, не коммить и не пушь. Ответ в чате дай по-русски. Все предлагаемые канонические документы, схемы, названия полей и нормативные формулировки должны быть на английском независимо от языка чата.

Возьми как вход:

1. Твой последний архитектурный вердикт о четырёх слоях, parity, shadow mode и vertical slice.
2. Внешний мастер-план:
   /Users/sashaabramovich/live-spec-codex/work/live-spec-vnext-master-roadmap.md
3. Существующие канонические документы LiveSpec — только адресно, через read-only workers. Не загружай их целиком в основную сессию.

Нужно подготовить исправленную архитектурную поправку, закрывающую следующие пробелы.

1. Full parity inventory

Не ограничивайся “representative rows”. Для каждой продуктовой возможности и каждого operational mechanism укажи:

- canonical source;
- specified;
- implemented;
- tested;
- installed;
- actually exercised;
- vNext owner;
- migration proof;
- fate: retain / consolidate / replace / defer / retire;
- fallback.

Не считай наличие текста доказательством реализации.

2. Documentation information architecture

Отдельно спроектируй документную архитектуру для:

- PRODUCT_SPEC.md;
- ARCHITECTURE.md;
- TEST_MATRIX.md;
- ROADMAP.md;
- DECISIONS.md;
- SURFACES.md;
- PROBLEMS.md;
- PROGRESS.md;
- OVERVIEW/README;
- skills and pipeline references.

Для каждого документа укажи:

- audience;
- purpose;
- canonical content;
- content that must not live there;
- duplicated material to remove or replace with links;
- what is always loaded;
- what is loaded on demand;
- readability budget or decomposition rule.

Readability is a product requirement, not cosmetic cleanup. Preserve scenarios, rationale, examples, exceptions and traceability, but organize them through progressive disclosure instead of one giant always-loaded body.

3. Human-facing work graph

Do not assume that ROADMAP notes alone are sufficient.

Reconcile the design with the existing work-board/product requirements, including Requirement 309 and related architecture/roadmap/decisions. Define how every meaningful chat message:

- attaches to an existing card or creates a new one;
- is classified as question, idea, feature, bug, decision, debt or local change;
- preserves provenance;
- exposes stage, owner, dependencies, pipeline, worktree, agents and evidence;
- records updates and history without making normal chat noisy;
- supports parallel and serial work;
- remains readable to a non-technical owner.

Do not invent a competing cards.yaml or second source of truth. First determine which existing canonical surface

Stop. Do not implement R0 yet.

Your second pass found useful technical facts, but it under-designed the human side of LiveSpec. Treat this as a correction to the architecture, not a request for a new kanban, persona system, YAML router or additional rule encyclopedia.

LiveSpec’s product promise is:

A person speaks naturally. The system gradually understands the person and the project, catches and stores meaningful work, validates what it can, performs routine work within consented boundaries, communicates at the person’s pace, preserves readable English canonical documents, and makes its current understanding easy to inspect, correct and revoke.

Design one missing layer: Adaptive onboarding and relationship model.

It must be lightweight and progressive:

- no mandatory questionnaire or feature tour;
- begin useful work immediately;
- ask only the smallest high-value question when uncertainty materially changes safety, cost or outcome;
- infer tentative preferences from interaction, but distinguish observed / inferred / confirmed / revoked;
- allow a person to inspect, correct, pause, delete or override every stored preference and inference;
- adapt language of chat, amount of detail, initiative, pace, approval thresholds, budget, reports and follow-up cadence;
- learn project type and local conventions from existing repository facts first, then ask targeted questions;
- preserve privacy: raw chat text is not automatically copied into durable task state; store a minimal summary/link/redacted form under explicit retention rules;
- support a new project, an existing non-LiveSpec project and an already adopted legacy LiveSpec project;
- explain “why I asked / why I acted / why this is waiting” in plain language;
- never silently broaden autonomy, external sharing, spending or durable retention.

Give this layer:

1. Its canonical owner(s), state model and lifecycle.
2. How it connects to L1 user profile, L2 project profile, L3 router, L4 execution policy and the work board.
3. The minimal data model, distinguishing durable facts from session-local observations.
4. Golden journeys:
   - first conversation on a new project;
   - existing project with docs/code to inspect;
   - user who wants terse updates;
   - user who changes preferences;
   - uncertain feature request;
   - sensitive/private message;
   - legacy LiveSpec project migration.
5. Proof and fallback for every automated inference.
6. Documentation placement using always / on-route / on-ask tiers.
7. Changes needed to the migration contract so existing projects preserve their useful history without importing old noise.

Return at most 900 words, in Russian, read-only. Use at most 3 read-only workers. Start with a verdict, then one integrated plan. No implementation proposal yet.

