message.content:
Stop architecture ideation. We now move from design to in-place canonical amendment planning.

Read only:
1. /Users/sashaabramovich/live-spec-codex/work/live-spec-vnext-master-roadmap.md
2. Targeted existing canonical sections needed for the task.

The external roadmap is a migration worksheet, never a new source of truth. Do not create a vNext spec, new roadmap, YAML router, board store, skill or implementation.

Prepare the first read-only canonical amendment map. Show exactly which existing clauses/nodes/rows must be retained, amended, superseded or linked for:

- progressive adaptive onboarding;
- confirmed versus session-local observations;
- privacy and retention;
- calibrated estimate ranges by task type/reach/route/project;
- estimate versus active/waiting/end-to-end actuals;
- legacy-host migration;
- document load tiers and readability;
- thin router and logical skill decoupling.

Use the existing canonical homes, especially:
- PRODUCT_SPEC Requirements 170, 171, 180–182, 186, 274 and 309;
- their existing ARCHITECTURE nodes and seams;
- corresponding TEST_MATRIX rows and tests;
- existing ROADMAP/DECISIONS entries.

For each amendment give:
- current canonical owner;
- existing behavior retained;
- exact contradiction or missing behavior;
- proposed English normative delta;
- architecture delta;
- proof/test delta;
- migration consequence;
- implementation priority.

Preserve existing anchors where possible. Do not duplicate accepted behavior into new sections.

Then propose atomic landing bundles ordered by:
1. reducing mandatory context;
2. preserving complete product and operational parity;
3. documentation readability;
4. shadow execution;
5. activation and host migration.

Return a compact diff plan in chat and wait for acceptance. No files, tests, commits, pushes or implementation. Avoid ceremonial “Корень” wording.
